        "text": "ered\n\"let's go inside for dinner my son\"\nand i nodded\nand locked your gaze\nas you coaxed me with your hands\nin to your embrace\n...Thoughts and memories\njust like above came rushing into me\nYou served unconditionally\nwithout reservation\nYou loved compassionately\nwithout hesitation\nWhen i was a child,\nI saw your cries ...\ni don't know the meaning then\nbut when i held your hand,\nyou hugged me tightly\nI was a witness to your laughter\nand you taught me to enjoy\nthe simple things in life\nMother, my de",
